    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The release note on its own [ev-971ffeb05b74] is vague, but the linked PR fills the gap. [ev-5236d3e631f7] says the PR adds a `--sparse-checkout-paths` flag, similar to `--ignore-paths`, to bring the sparse checkout feature from 2.6.0 to the CLI. [ev-2a263ee924fe] shows the change only touches cmd/flux/create_source_git.go and its tests, so the subject is a new flag on `flux create source git` (change: added). That is enough to write the subject and applicability: the flag is optional, so only people who choose to use it are affected, and existing setups see no change if the operator does nothing.",
